<!-- ====================== LAWS ===================== -->
<!-- ================================================= -->

<section id="laws" class="tab-content">

<h2 class="section-title">
Newton's Laws of Motion
</h2>


<div class="card">

<h2>Newton's First Law</h2>

<p>
An object remains at rest or continues to move with uniform
velocity in a straight line unless acted upon by an external
unbalanced force.
</p>

<div class="formula">
F<sub>net</sub> = 0 → a = 0
</div>

<div class="success">
This law is also called the <strong>Law of Inertia</strong>.
</div>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>Newton's Second Law</h2>

<p>
The rate of change of momentum of an object is proportional
to the applied force and occurs in the direction of that force.
</p>

<div class="formula">
F = ma
</div>

<div class="formula">
F = Δp/Δt
</div>

<div class="info">
For constant mass:
<strong>F = ma</strong>
</div>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>Newton's Third Law</h2>

<p>
For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.
</p>

<div class="formula">
F<sub>AB</sub> = −F<sub>BA</sub>
</div>

<div class="warning">
Action and reaction act on <strong>different objects</strong>,
so they do not cancel each other.
</div>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>Newton's Laws — Quick Comparison</h2>

<div class="table-wrap">

<table>

<tr>
<th>Law</th>
<th>Main Concept</th>
<th>Key Point</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>First Law</td>
<td>Inertia</td>
<td>Net force zero → no acceleration</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Second Law</td>
<td>Acceleration</td>
<td>F = ma</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Third Law</td>
<td>Action-Reaction</td>
<td>Equal and opposite forces</td>
</tr>

</table>

</div>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>Applications of Newton's Laws</h2>

<div class="accordion">

<button onclick="toggleAccordion(this)">
Why do passengers move forward when a bus suddenly stops?
</button>

<div class="accordion-content">
<p>
Due to inertia of motion, the passenger's body tends to
continue moving forward when the bus stops suddenly.
</p>
</div>

</div>


<div class="accordion">

<button onclick="toggleAccordion(this)">
Why does a gun recoil after firing?
</button>

<div class="accordion-content">
<p>
The bullet moves forward and an equal and opposite momentum
is produced in the gun, causing recoil.
</p>
</div>

</div>


<div class="accordion">

<button onclick="toggleAccordion(this)">
Why can we walk?
</button>

<div class="accordion-content">
<p>
Our foot pushes the ground backward. The ground exerts an
equal and opposite frictional force on us, pushing us forward.
</p>
</div>

</div>


<div class="accordion">

<button onclick="toggleAccordion(this)">
Why does a rocket move upward?
</button>

<div class="accordion-content">
<p>
The rocket pushes gases downward. The gases exert an equal
and opposite force on the rocket, producing upward motion.
</p>
</div>

</div>

</div>

</section>


