<div class="card">

<h2>🔥 Trick 1 — Force</h2>

<div class="formula">
Force = Mass × Acceleration
</div>

<p>
Whenever mass and acceleration are given, directly use F = ma.
</p>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>🔥 Trick 2 — Weight vs Mass</h2>

<div class="formula">
Mass → kg
</div>

<div class="formula">
Weight → N
</div>

<div class="warning">
Do not confuse mass with weight.
Weight is a force.
</div>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>🔥 Trick 3 — Momentum</h2>

<div class="formula">
Momentum = mv
</div>

<p>
Mass × velocity = momentum.
</p>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>🔥 Trick 4 — Impulse</h2>

<div class="formula">
Impulse = Force × Time
</div>

<p>
Impulse is also equal to change in momentum.
</p>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>🔥 Trick 5 — Same Direction</h2>

<div class="formula">
Same Direction → Add
</div>

<p>
Example: 20 N + 30 N = 50 N
</p>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>🔥 Trick 6 — Opposite Direction</h2>

<div class="formula">
Opposite Direction → Subtract
</div>

<p>
Example: 50 N − 20 N = 30 N
</p>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>🔥 Trick 7 — Newton's Laws</h2>

<div class="formula">
1st → Inertia
</div>

<div class="formula">
2nd → F = ma
</div>

<div class="formula">
3rd → Action & Reaction
</div>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>🔥 Trick 8 — Friction</h2>

<div class="formula">
Rolling friction &lt; Sliding friction
</div>

<p>
Therefore wheels are used to reduce friction.
</p>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>🔥 Trick 9 — Net Force Zero</h2>

<div class="formula">
F<sub>net</sub> = 0 → a = 0
</div>

<p>
The object may still be moving with constant velocity.
</p>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>⚠️ Common Exam Traps</h2>

<ul>

<li>
Force is a vector quantity.
</li>

<li>
Mass is a scalar quantity.
</li>

<li>
Weight is a force.
</li>

<li>
Newton's First Law is the law of inertia.
</li>

<li>
Newton's Second Law gives F = ma for constant mass.
</li>

<li>
Action and reaction act on different bodies.
</li>

<li>
Momentum is mass × velocity.
</li>

<li>
Impulse equals change in momentum.
</li>

<li>
Balanced force does not mean the object must be at rest.
</li>

<li>
Zero net force means zero acceleration, not necessarily zero velocity.
</li>

</ul>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>⭐ One-Minute Revision</h2>

<div class="formula">
F = ma
</div>

<div class="formula">
p = mv
</div>

<div class="formula">
J = FΔt = Δp
</div>

<div class="formula">
W = mg
</div>

<div class="formula">
F = Gm₁m₂/r²
</div>

<div class="formula">
f = μN
</div>

<div class="success">
<strong>1st Law:</strong> Inertia<br>
<strong>2nd Law:</strong> F = ma<br>
<strong>3rd Law:</strong> Action = Reaction
</div>

</div>

